Workstream ID: ai-architect-agent-cloud
Title: Agent-native cloud specialization for the AI Architect roadmap
Status: IN_PROGRESS
Milestone: Extend Neural Edge with bounded, verifiable agent-cloud architecture
Dependencies: versioned-roadmaps, career-graph, discovery-atlas
GitHub issue: https://github.com/Zanark/CareerOS/issues/11
Purpose: Add research-backed learning to the existing AI Architect mission, not a
  separate mission. Keep the original curriculum, genuine evidence and old saved
  positions intact. Distinguish machine-programmable cloud from infrastructure
  for agents and cloud engineering/operations by agents.

Tasks:
  [x] Review public primary evidence and trace the existing Neural Edge curriculum.
  [x] Author twelve checkpoints, four independent cases and meaningful exercises.
  [x] Preserve the frozen v3 curriculum and use explicit verified v3-to-v4 append.
  [x] Integrate mixed PDF/web citations, library/search, roadmap and transfer links.
  [x] Preserve source-derived Atlas, records, backups and encrypted journal behavior.
  [x] Add a final tutorial explanation and focused usage/research documentation.
  [x] Qualify compatibility and real isolated desktop/phone workflows.
  [x] Preview, apply and independently read back the same issue/Project mapping.
  [ ] Commit and push the reviewed public-safe source with verified attribution.
  [ ] Qualify the exact GitHub Pages run, artifact and actual hosted extension.
  [ ] Reconcile final publication evidence on this same issue and Project item.

Acceptance criteria:
  Neural Edge retains its original 28 checkpoints and adds 12 research checkpoints.
  Existing v3 trackers do not switch until confirmed adoption; verified identical
    prefix work carries once, with exact archived progress and no new free credit.
  Other editions, missions, saved modes, focus, dates and records remain unchanged.
  Learning covers runtime/isolation, identity/policy, durable side effects, tools/
    context, coding/operations, release/recovery, evaluation, latency and economics.
  All added material has actual primary web citations and honest reviewed limits.
    No synthetic PDF page number or vendor benchmark is invented.
  Four optional cases remain independently browsable, not completion gates.
  No paid account, real customer data or production access is mandatory.
  The local preview remains available; qualification never drives a real profile.
  Technical completion, owner acceptance and source publication stay separate.
  The initial implementation authorized local work and adopted tracking only.
    The owner's separate November 10 push/deploy request authorizes reviewed
    source publication through the existing main-branch Pages workflow.
  Deployment must match its actual successful source/run/artifact and preserve
    explicit adoption, saved progress, private PDFs and the empty public journal.
    It does not authorize cloud experiments or public upload of research PDFs.

Completion evidence:
  Research basis: reviewed public platform/protocol documentation, company
    engineering reports, empirical studies and a conventional-automation incident.
  Implementation: Neural v4 has 40 checkpoints/88 units/869 exercises; original
    28-checkpoint/72-unit/809-exercise source remains unchanged. Four additional
    cited transfer links and five tutorial lessons preserve prior identities.
  Qualification: TypeScript, 712 unit cases and 22 tracking cases pass. The initial
    63-case native run passed 58 and found five fixture/selector failures; the
    focused eight-case correction passes all five, with 63 unique cases qualified.
    All 182 tutorial steps pass at 1440/390/320 pixels. Real v4 evidence survives
    ordinary export/import and old-v3 encrypted baseline/new-v4 append replay.
  Scoped evidence: docs/tracking/2026-11-10-agent-cloud-local-qualification.json.
    Two actual dark-desktop/light-phone source frames reviewed; no user approval,
    production benchmark or complete fresh browser/hosted suite is inferred.
  Completion mapping: review preview/apply and an independent API read agree on
    issue 11 and original Project 4 item PVTI_lAHOAe2wCs4BqeZyzhHRivE.
    Final closed/completed/Done read-back is retained separately in the completion
    apply/no-op receipts under docs/tracking. Preserve these identities.
  Publication: separately authorized November 10; source commit/push, exact Pages
    gate and hosted verification are pending, not implied by earlier local checks.

